#X text 1450 900 size is the combs' feedback \, one for all eight as in Freeverb \, worked out so the tail measures the time e_verb's size reads: 0.5 s at 0 to 10 s at 100 \, even in ratio. damping is Freeverb's: the low-passes' pole from 0 at 0 to 0.4 at 100 \, its damp 0 to 1. Each starts at 50 in its boxes: c_steps tells c_kit every value at load. The gain is Freeverb's \, 0.015 in for each of two inputs and 3 out \, with what matches its level to the plate's \, falling a little as size grows \, since a longer tail makes freeverb louder than it makes the plate., f 50;
#X text 1450 1180 The engine's own: the input at its gain while it is wanted and 0 once it is not \, so a type changed away from rings out on what it already holds \; e_tail turns its switch~ on while it is wanted and off once its tail has died \, clearing its delay lines \, and the outlet tells e_verb \, whose own switch~ is on while any engine is., f 50;
